{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For the iniquity — and I struck him.</b> Return to My people mentioned above, or to the broken and lowly of spirit. And <b>אכהו</b> (I struck him) is a verb indicating future tense, for it has no sign for it in the sacred language:" "<b>I hid.</b> I hid My face and struck him by hand, by way of parable, until I do not have compassion on him. And behold, <b>הסתר</b> is a verb name:" "<b>[And he went wayward].</b> He went wayward, contending and growing stronger, and returned to his evil way. And the word <b>שובב</b> is pejorative:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 57, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:01.504335467Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}